		    Type		    "Zone Comparator"
		    Description		    "This block performs the zone comparison. Its inputs are the resistance and reactance signals. "
		    "Four forward and one backward zones are implemented. The output that corresponds to the zone where the impedance"
		    " is located is set to one while the rest of the outputs are zero Either the mho or free expression characteristi"
		    "cs may be set. For the mho characteristic, the zones are defined by specifying the center of each circle (all th"
		    "e circles are tangent to the origin). For the free expression, arrays with consecutive vertices specify the poly"
		    "gons for each zone."
		    Help		    "\n\n"
		    Initialization	    "zc1;\n"
		    Display		    "plot(x1(:,1),x1(:,2));\nplot(x2(:,1),x2(:,2));\nplot(x3(:,1),x3(:,2));\nplot(x4(:,1),x4(:,2));\npl"
